cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GUS, please cite it as below."
title: "Gerarion Universal Standard (GUS 3.0.0): calendario computacional y proyecto de interoperabilidad temporal y evidencias verificables"
version: 3.2.2
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - CC0-1.0
authors:
  - name: "verared"
    website: "https://github.com/verared"
  - name: "Gerardo Loyola"
    website: "https://github.com/geroiloyola"
abstract: "GUS defines a regular calendar kernel (364-day common year, 371-day Gran Tempalum year) plus a continuous instant scale (TCJ = TAI + 8,400 s) and an optional GST v2 cryptographic sealing layer (hybrid Ed25519 + ML-DSA over RFC 8785 JCS). Three independent implementations (Python, JavaScript, C11) conform to a single normative vector set."
keywords:
  - calendar
  - timestamp
  - post-quantum
  - cryptography
  - time
repository-code: "https://github.com/verared/gerarion"
